hortName":"E. Gudbranson"},"type":"defender"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1828","fullName":"Nationwide Arena","address":{"city":"Columbus","state":"OH","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1828.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":14134,"officials":[{"fullName":"Tom Chmielewski","displayName":"Tom Chmielewski","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kyle Flemington","displayName":"Kyle Flemington","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Mike Sullivan","displayName":"Mike Sullivan","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jeremy Faucher","displayName":"Jeremy Faucher","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Bennett scores twice as Panthers stop 2-game skid with a 4-1 win over Blue Jackets","description":"— Sam Bennett scored twice, and the Florida Panthers snapped a two-game skid with a 4-1 win over the Columbus Blue Jackets on Tuesday night.","story":"COLUMBUS, Ohio -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114732/sam-bennett\">Sam Bennett</a> scored twice, and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/fla/florida-panthers\">Florida Panthers</a> snapped a two-game skid with a 4-1 win over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cbj/columbus-blue-jackets\">Columbus Blue Jackets</a> on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Florida notched its 12th victory in the last 13 games against the Blue Jackets.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3946/lars-eller\">Lars Eller</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114722/sam-reinhart\">Sam Reinhart</a> also scored. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114717/aaron-ekblad\">Aaron Ekblad</a> had three assists, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697395/anton-lundell\">Anton Lundell</a> added two assists. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5452/jacob-markstrom\">Jacob Markstrom</a> stopped 37 shots for Florida, which improved to 6-0-0 when leading after two periods.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899939/ivan-provorov\">Ivan Provorov</a> scored for the Blue Jackets. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5734/cam-talbot\">Cam Talbot</a> stopped 24 shots.\n\n\r\n              Bennett opened the scoring with a power-play goal off the rush at the two-minute mark of the second period, giving Florida a power-play goal in seven of its last eight games.\n\n\r\n              Eller made it 2-0 at 4:17 before Provorov cut that lead in half with 20 seconds left in the period.\n\n\r\n              Bennett restored the two-goal lead at 14:29 of the third. Matthew Tkachuk’s assist was his team-leading 23rd and extended both his assist and point streaks to five games. \n\n\r\n              Reinhart capped the scoring with an empty-net goal at 17:44, his 17th score and 43rd point in 32 career games against Columbus.\n\n\r\n              The Blue Jackets have been outscored 23-8 in the middle frame through 16 games this season and are 0-9-0 when trailing after two periods.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Panthers: Host Detroit on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Blue Jackets: Host Tampa Bay on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-11T16:26:43Z"}}